‎
‎## 5. The Ledger — Choices Have Consequences
‎
‎> A choice contains promise and danger simultaneously. Consequences often become visible years later.
‎
‎**Choice ledger:**
‎
‎- **Choice:** Remain destination (portal) — Promise: retain users, ad revenue now. Danger: mechanism underneath becomes more valuable than destination.
‎- **Choice:** Use Google search inside Yahoo — Promise: better results now. Danger: train users that Google is infrastructure, make Google credible, weaken own network effects.
‎- **Choice:** Not acquire Google — Promise: focus on core. Danger: competitor becomes infrastructure you depend on.
‎- **Choice:** Later build own search — Promise: compete. Danger: landscape already shifted, switching costs for users now reversed.
‎
‎**History became ledger of consequences.**
‎
‎This is [[Digital_Frontier_Dispatch_014_Choices]]:
‎> Choices have consequences — Choice → Consequence → Feedback → Learning
‎
‎Yahoo case = consequence visible years later. Crossroads didn't announce:
‎
‎> THIS IS THE DECISION THAT WILL DEFINE YOUR FUTURE.
‎
‎It simply presented alternatives.
‎
