‎
‎## 6. HakunaShortcut Formulation — Sharper
‎
‎> You don't always lose because you made the wrong choice. Sometimes you lose because you correctly understood the present — and incorrectly understood where the road was going.
‎
‎**Operating translation for KQ:**
‎
‎| Present Understanding | Future Misunderstanding | Result |
‎| :--- | :--- | :--- |
‎| Portal is valuable now | Mechanism becomes infrastructure later | Lose future |
‎| Keeping users inside is monetizable | Getting out of way is more valuable mechanism | Lose navigation layer |
‎| Search is feature of portal | Search IS navigation | Lose business definition |
‎
‎**Links to [[Rule_06_Layer]]:**
‎- Locate your layer before you build strategy
‎- Yahoo mis-located: thought it was top layer (destination), but mechanism underneath became new top layer
‎
‎**Links to [[Rule_08_Portability]]:**
‎- Yahoo's workflows, knowledge, outputs could not travel to new forest (mechanism forest)
‎- Google's could — find and get out of way travels everywhere
‎
‎**Links to [[Rule_10_Protocol]]:**
‎- Yahoo: interface (portal pages)
‎- Google: protocol (search = command → navigate)
‎
‎Protocol beats interface when forest grows.
‎
