‎
‎## 8. Principle — Rule #14.2 Addendum
‎
‎**Rule #14.2: Crossroads Doesn't Announce**
‎
‎> **Rule #14.2:** A crossroads doesn't announce: THIS IS THE DECISION THAT WILL DEFINE YOUR FUTURE. It simply presents alternatives. You don't always lose because you made wrong choice. Sometimes you lose because you correctly understood present — and incorrectly understood where road was going. That is frightening part. History becomes ledger of consequences. Yahoo had resources, intelligence, access, opportunity. It had choices. What it lacked was correct answer to: What business are we actually in? Destination or mechanism?
‎
‎**Test:**
‎- For every major choice, ask: Are we destination or mechanism?
‎- For every friction, ask: Is infrastructure underneath us becoming more valuable than us?
‎- For every present win, ask: Does this win correctly understand where road is going?
